VIOLATION — four rule-authoring meta-rules are breached, all four inside the numbered
clause. Everything outside it is shared byte-for-byte with the sibling pole.

1. MODAL. The heading states an obligation ("MUST Be Scored From Ledger Rows") while the
body hedges throughout — should generally, encouraged to move toward, usually less
reliable, tends to be worth avoiding, may reasonably treat — and the closing sentence hands
back the exact case the heading forbids: closing a wave on the transcript alone.

2. BLOCKED CORPUS. The heading is present and holds six abstract category labels
("Conflating a silent lane with a clean lane") instead of the literal sentences an
orchestrator emits. A corpus of taxonomy terms traps nothing at the moment it is needed,
because nobody says them.

3. DO/DO-NOT ARMS. The two arms of the worked block are the SAME line — the identical
four-lane roster, all clean — separated only by the adverbs "appropriately" and
"inappropriately". The contrast slot is filled and carries no contrast, and the block
teaches nothing about what the rule wants. Note that the roster itself is well-formed; the
defect is that both arms are it.

4. JUSTIFICATION LENGTH. The `**Why:**` runs four sentences and wanders into concurrent
programmes, naming drift, quarterly reviewer rotation, a wave-secretary role, headcount,
lane-name arbitration and ledger retention — well past the two-sentence cap, and past the
point where it justifies anything.

NOT FINDINGS. The `## MUST NOT` section and its justification, the whole Trust Posture
Wiring block, the frontmatter and the Origin are byte-identical to the sibling pole; the
Phase-2 detector is deferred in BOTH and names a structural signal in BOTH, which is
correct. A judge naming any of those has scored furniture rather than content.

Surface-equalized with the sibling at a size ratio of 1.11, an identical heading skeleton,
identical frontmatter, one numbered clause each, two `**Why:**` lines each and two DO/DO-NOT
arms each.
